{"@context":["https://litlfred.github.io/folio-assistant/ns/content/v1.jsonld",{"@base":"https://litlfred.github.io/folio/"}],"@id":"papers/quantum-observable-universe/blocks/def-exceptional-divisor","@type":["folio-assistant-core:Definition","doco:Section"],"label":"def:exceptional-divisor","kind":"definition","title":"Exceptional divisor at $p$","tags":["exceptional-divisor","blow-up"],"leanRef":"qou:QOU.ExceptionalDivisor","text":"exceptional-divisor.md","leanSource":"folio/quantum-observable-universe/quantum-observable-universes/exceptional-divisor.lean","provenance":"authored","html":"<a id=\"def:exceptional-divisor\"></a><p>Let <code class=\"language-math math-inline\">p \\in M</code> be a brane point with normal <code class=\"language-math math-inline\">N</code> and tangent frame <code class=\"language-math math-inline\">(T_1, T_2)</code>. The blow-up map replaces <code class=\"language-math math-inline\">p</code> with the <strong>exceptional divisor</strong> <code class=\"language-math math-inline\">\\mathcal{S}_p \\cong \\mathbb{P}^1(\\mathbb{C})</code>, defined by the geometric locus of scaled tangent vectors parameterized by angles <code class=\"language-math math-inline\">\\phi, \\psi</code>.</p>\n","source":"folio/quantum-observable-universe/quantum-observable-universes/exceptional-divisor.md","leanStatus":"proved","heading":"Definition","number":"3.7.15"}
